[size=6][b][color=#AC6EE2]Hellraiser Revival's Ketamine Menu[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4]The all-in-one in-game trainer for Clive Barker's Hellraiser: Revival.[/size]
[size=3]One file. Press [b][color=#F89FCD]Insert[/color][/b] or [b][color=#F89FCD]F8[/color][/b]. Done.[/size]

[url=https://github.com/literalynn/Hellraiser-Revivals-Ketamine-Menu][b]Source code on GitHub[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://github.com/literalynn/Hellraiser-Revivals-Ketamine-Menu/releases][b]Releases[/b][/url]  ·  [url=https://github.com/literalynn/Hellraiser-Revivals-Ketamine-Menu/issues][b]Report a bug[/b][/url][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#F89FCD]Why this one[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]One DLL, nothing else.[/b] No UE4SS, no Cheat Engine, no launcher, no Visual C++ redistributable.
[*][b]No game file modified.[/b] Uninstalling is deleting one file.
[*][b]Several mods in one.[/b] Trainer, silent aim, FOV editor, free camera, ESP, item spawner, auto lockpick and intro skip in a single menu.
[*][b]Clean overlay.[/b] A real in-game menu (DirectX 12 and 11), mouse and keyboard, with tooltips on every option.
[*][b]9 languages.[/b] English, 简体中文, 日本語, 한국어, Русский, Deutsch, Français, Español, Português (Brasil). It follows your Windows language; change it in Settings.
[*][b]Zero footprint when closed.[/b] Nothing is drawn and your input is untouched, apart from the ESP and hotkeys you turn on.
[*][b]Update-proof by design.[/b] It finds the game's data by name at runtime. If an update removes something, that option is greyed out with the reason, instead of crashing your game.
[*][b]Open source (MIT).[/b] Every release is built from the public code by GitHub Actions.
[/list]

