[size=4][b][color=#AC6EE2]Full feature list[/color][/b][/size]
[spoiler]
[b]Player[/b]
[list]
[*]God mode, infinite health, health slider (set any value)
[*]No sprint cooldown (the game has no stamina)
[*]Invisible to enemies
[*]One-hit kill, damage multiplier
[/list]
[b]Combat[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Silent aim:[/b] your shots hit the head of the enemy nearest the crosshair, inside an adjustable circle (shown or hidden from the ESP tab)
[*]Infinite ammo, unbreakable melee weapons
[*]Genesis Configuration powers with no Suffering cost, no power cooldown, refill Suffering
[*][b]Unlock powers early:[/b] Telekinesis, Pyrokinesis and Hellchains, before the story gives them
[/list]
[b]Movement[/b]
[list]
[*]Fly and noclip towards where you look, with your usual movement keys or gamepad
[*]Free camera (your character stays in place)
[*]Speed and jump height multipliers
[*]3 saved positions + teleport to any level checkpoint
[/list]
[b]ESP[/b]
[list]
[*]Enemies: box, health bar, name, distance, skeleton, head marker, chams, snaplines, off-screen arrows
[*]World: items on the ground, loot containers, save points
[*]Separate range for enemies and objects
[/list]
[b]Inventory[/b]
[list]
[*]Add or remove money
[*]Give any item in any amount: ammo, weapons, upgrades, healing, materials (list built from the game itself)
[*]Unlock weapon skins & charms
[/list]
[b]World[/b]
[list]
[*]Time scale (slow motion / fast forward)
[*]Freeze enemies, kill enemies nearby
[*][b]FOV editor:[/b] lock the field of view anywhere from 50° to 130°, live. [i]Game default[/i] gives control back to the game.
[*]Hide HUD
[*][b]Auto lockpick:[/b] locks open by themselves a moment after you start picking them
[/list]
[b]Progress[/b]
[list]
[*]See active and completed objectives, complete one, change the shop level
[/list]
[b]Settings[/b]
[list]
[*]A hotkey for any switch (works with the menu closed, with a small notification)
[*]Two rebindable menu keys (Insert and F8), 9 languages, UI scale, settings saved automatically
[*][b]Skip intros:[/b] no logos or notices at startup (about 30 s saved)
[*]Footer with game version, CPU, GPU, RAM, resolution and FPS
[/list]
[/spoiler]

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#F89FCD]Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Vortex:[/b] click [b]Mod Manager Download[/b], then enable and deploy. Vortex puts it in the right folder by itself.

[b]Manual:[/b]
[list=1]
[*]In Steam: right-click the game → [i]Manage[/i] → [i]Browse local files[/i].
[*]Extract the zip [b]into that folder[/b] (the one that contains the [i]Hellraiser[/i] folder). You should end up with:
[code]Hellraiser\Binaries\Win64\winmm.dll[/code]
next to [i]Hellraiser-Win64-Shipping.exe[/i].
[*]Start the game, load a save, press [b]Insert[/b] or [b]F8[/b].
[/list]
[b]Linux / Steam Deck (Proton):[/b] Proton loads its own [i]winmm.dll[/i] instead of the menu's. In Steam, right-click the game → [i]Properties[/i] → [i]Launch Options[/i] and add:
[code]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="winmm=n,b" %command%[/code]

[size=4][b][color=#AC6EE2]Before you play[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Back up your saves[/b] first: [i]%LOCALAPPDATA%\Hellraiser\Saved\SaveGames[/i]
[*]Giving key items or completing objectives can break scripted sequences: [b]save before you use them[/b].
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#F89FCD]Compatibility[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Game:[/b] 1.1.1.227384 (October 2026 update) and 1.0.1.227219, Steam.
[*][b]Renderer:[/b] DirectX 12 (default) and DirectX 11.
[*][b]Linux / Steam Deck:[/b] works through Proton with the launch option above.
[*][b]Other mods:[/b] uses [i]winmm.dll[/i], so it works alongside ReShade ([i]dxgi.dll[/i]) and UE4SS ([i]dwmapi.dll[/i]).
[*][b]Frame generation[/b] (DLSS-G, FSR, XeSS FG): supported. If the menu flickers, turn frame generation off.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#AC6EE2]Uninstall[/color][/b][/size]
[b]Vortex:[/b] remove the mod, then delete [i]KetamineMenu.ini[/i] and [i]KetamineMenu.log[/i] that the menu created.
[b]Manual:[/b] delete [i]winmm.dll[/i], [i]KetamineMenu-LICENSE.txt[/i], [i]KetamineMenu.ini[/i] and [i]KetamineMenu.log[/i] from [i]Hellraiser\Binaries\Win64[/i].

[line]

[size=4][b][color=#F89FCD]Troubleshooting[/color][/b][/size]
[spoiler]
[b]Insert / F8 do nothing[/b]
Check that [i]winmm.dll[/i] is in [i]Hellraiser\Binaries\Win64[/i], not in the top game folder. Open [i]KetamineMenu.log[/i] in the same folder: if it doesn't exist, the DLL wasn't loaded (check the folder and your antivirus).

[b]Everything is greyed out[/b]
Load a save first: most options need the player to exist. If the header says [i]Engine not hooked[/i], the game version changed in a way the menu can't handle yet: post in the Bugs tab with your [i]KetamineMenu.log[/i].

[b]My antivirus flags the DLL[/b]
Trainers hook into a game's rendering and memory, which antivirus heuristics dislike. It's a false positive: the full source code is on GitHub and every release is built from it by GitHub Actions. You can also build it yourself.
[/spoiler]

[b]Found a bug?[/b] Use the Bugs tab or [url=https://github.com/literalynn/Hellraiser-Revivals-Ketamine-Menu/issues]GitHub issues[/url], with what you did, what happened, and your [i]KetamineMenu.log[/i] (overwritten each time the game starts).

